## PR type
Bug fix (documentation build)

## What does this PR do?
Fixes #<issue号>

## Problem
On readthedocs, the four "Supported Hardware" reference links on the
installation page (AMD/NPU/MetaX/MUSA) point to raw
`../BestPractices/*-support.md` paths and 404. The in-table distillation-docs
link in `Megatron-SWIFT/GKD.md` is broken the same way (5 links total).

## Root cause
`sphinx_markdown_tables` pre-converts Markdown tables into raw HTML, so MyST
never rewrites relative `.md` links inside table cells to `.html`. The
extension dates back to the recommonmark era (2023, #77); myst_parser handles
pipe tables natively, making the extension redundant and harmful.

## Fix
Remove `sphinx_markdown_tables` from:
- `docs/source/conf.py`
- `docs/source_en/conf.py`
- `requirements/docs.txt`

## Experiment results

Commands (run at repo root):

```
pip install -r requirements/docs.txt
sphinx-build -b html docs/source /tmp/out-zh
sphinx-build -b html docs/source_en /tmp/out-en
pre-commit run --all-files
```

Results:
- Hardware links render as `BestPractices/{AMD,NPU,Metax,MUSA}-support.html`
  in both zh and en trees (verified via grep on generated HTML)
- GKD in-table link renders as `../Instruction/Distillation.html#...`
- Table count unchanged: 69 tables in both trees before/after (no rendering
  regression)
- Full-tree scan: remaining raw `.md` hrefs are only legit `_sources/*.md.txt`
  viewer links and external links
- `pre-commit run --all-files`: all checks passed

